<article class="env-lemma" id="05F3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05F3">Lemma <span data-tag="05F3">32.4.9</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/086P" data-tag="086P">32.4.5</a>. Suppose we are given an $i$ and a morphism $T \to S_ i$ such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$T \times _{S_ i} S = \emptyset $, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$T$ is quasi-compact. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $T \times _{S_ i} S_{i'} = \emptyset $ for all sufficiently large $i'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/01YZ" data-tag="01YZ">32.2.3</a> we see that $T \times _{S_ i} S = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits _{i' \geq i} T \times _{S_ i} S_{i'}$. Hence the result follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/01Z2" data-tag="01Z2">32.4.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>